From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:36:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: report no collapsible browser controls to Blink

ContentWebState reports the collapsible part of Chrome's top and bottom
toolbars to Blink as browser controls (30 pt and 78 pt from the insets
CRCWebViewportContainerView hard-codes), the way Chrome for Android
hides its toolbar while scrolling. Blink therefore lets the page scroll
that much further than its viewport, expecting the controls to collapse
and reveal the rest. They never do: FullscreenMediator ignores scrolls
the scroll view is not dragging, and with Blink that scroll view only
mirrors Blink's offset. So the last 108 pt of every page stayed hidden
under the bottom toolbar.

Report no collapsible controls, so Blink's maximum scroll offset matches
the visible area. The toolbars stay as they were; making them collapse
would need Blink's scrolling wired into Chrome's fullscreen logic.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c in the iOS 27 simulator with a
page that shows scrollY and its bottom element: before, scrolling
stopped 108 px short of the maximum with the last element under the
toolbar; after, the page scrolls to the maximum, the last element shows
in full, and nothing is hidden at the top.

diff --git a/ios/web/content/web_state/content_web_state.mm b/ios/web/content/web_state/content_web_state.mm
index a131057bb8c15415bc9a722fc36a396a80530d7a..cd069d418751a900a74a4a3cbfadad6da37436a7 100644
--- a/ios/web/content/web_state/content_web_state.mm
+++ b/ios/web/content/web_state/content_web_state.mm
@@ -791,11 +791,13 @@ void SerializeMetadata(web::proto::WebStateMetadataStorage& metadata) {
 }
 
 int ContentWebState::GetTopControlsHeight() {
-  return ([web_view_ maxViewportInsets].top -
-          [web_view_ minViewportInsets].top) *
-         display::Screen::Get()
-             ->GetDisplayNearestWindow(web_contents_->GetTopLevelNativeWindow())
-             .device_scale_factor();
+  // [ios-blink-sideload] Chrome's toolbars never collapse over Blink content:
+  // FullscreenMediator ignores scrolls the scroll view is not dragging, and
+  // that scroll view only mirrors Blink's offset. Reporting collapsible
+  // controls makes Blink keep their height as extra scroll range, which then
+  // stays hidden under the toolbar: the bottom of every page (108 pt with the
+  // insets CRCWebViewportContainerView hard-codes) could not be reached.
+  return 0;
 }
 
 int ContentWebState::GetTopControlsMinHeight() {
@@ -803,11 +805,8 @@ void SerializeMetadata(web::proto::WebStateMetadataStorage& metadata) {
 }
 
 int ContentWebState::GetBottomControlsHeight() {
-  return ([web_view_ maxViewportInsets].bottom -
-          [web_view_ minViewportInsets].bottom) *
-         display::Screen::Get()
-             ->GetDisplayNearestWindow(web_contents_->GetTopLevelNativeWindow())
-             .device_scale_factor();
+  // [ios-blink-sideload] See GetTopControlsHeight().
+  return 0;
 }
 
 int ContentWebState::GetBottomControlsMinHeight() {
